  "limitations": [
    "Automated native Windows CLI/import/runner and graph validation; no desktop GUI acceptance or institutional approval claim.",
    "Small synthetic known-answer and rejection tests; no human-scale memory/performance benchmark or clinical validation.",
    "Offline imports verify the complete payload inventory and duplicate-version immutability; publisher identity is not authenticated by these hashes and catalogue publication is a separate action.",
    "SnpEff consequence predictions and ANN impact selection do not establish pathogenicity. Impact selection retains entire records, including all alternate alleles, genotypes and existing FILTER values.",
    "Local VCF annotation requires explicitly matching assemblies and normalized biallelic records; header checks cannot prove absent assembly identities and no liftover occurs.",
    "Reference/annotation databases are selected local resources with explicit genetic codes and per-contig overrides; only a tiny synthetic database is bundled, not a human biological reference.",
    "Only unused javax/vecmath entries are omitted from upstream JAR containers; retained scientific classes/resources match the official core byte for byte. Structural/PDB operations are outside the supported scope.",
    "Pinned SnpSift v5.4b source is the latest upstream source before the official 5.4c core build; its displayed version derives from SnpEff. This is source correspondence, not a claim of a bit-reproducible upstream compiler environment.",
    "Private executables run trusted native code. Disabled upstream downloads/telemetry/update checks are not a network or execution sandbox."
  ],
